{
  "about": "tauri-plugin-sew-voice 0.3.0: the exact VoiceListener calls a native shim (CallKit, Telecom) gets, scenario by scenario. Each step is what the host or Sew does ('do'), then every listener call that follows, in order, as {\"<method>\": <argument as JSON>}; the arguments serialise as the sew-voice:// events do (on_self_mute's is SelfMute). Every call but on_self_mute follows the webview event with the same payload. tests/listener.rs drives the fake engine through VoiceControl with these steps and checks the calls are exactly these. Member ids, target and room are the tests' (as in native-voice-contract.json); 1001 started the recording.",
  "sew": "0.7.3",
  "plugin": "0.3.0",
  "scenarios": {
    "held_join": {
      "about": "A join into a recorded room. Sew refuses it with 409 recording_consent_required, so the plugin holds it: join answers call_id \"\", then on_state(consent_required) and on_recording with Sew's notice (consent_prompt; ConsentPrompt::title_en(ConsentAsk::Join) and text_en give the kit's words). No microphone, no media, no keys. VoiceControl::consent(true, notice_version) joins again with the answer: the held notice clears (on_recording(null)), your row arrives, the call connects, and Sew's recording follows with my_consent granted. To give up instead (your 30 s timer), call leave().",
